      "closure_rationale": "Parsed copied grammar descriptors and typed argument factories separate syntax, category and lifetime enforcement. Complete preparation precedes bounded sink admission, so rejected appends preserve every byte and used; copied streaming messages instead retain exact accepted progress, which cannot be rolled back externally. The ten-digit uint32 and128-byte DSL message bounds are derived under explicit ASCII/octet premises; retained text termination differs from bounded spans. Actual GCC/Clang category negatives have executing positives, and G++/Clang++ C++20-mode experiments reject incompatible literals while runtime vformat throws. The inspected rolling draft is not mislabeled published C++20. Six profiles pass four named anchors, eight compiled semantic controls including actual retained MOD15/16, and four compiling learner stubs reject. An independent regex/substitution/immutable-prefix oracle matches12812cases:7240formats,5572stream histories and1527accepted formats; capacities0..11 and guard suffixes are separately checked. Required parsed DSL and partial writer support implements copied32-byte formats/128-byte messages, repeated typed placeholders, exact prefix offsets, zero-progress backpressure, errors after acceptance, cancellation and protocol-uncertainty terminal states. Four actual local nonblocking-pipe executions observe EAGAIN then offsets0/2/4/5 and no post-cancel output; callbacks remain synchronous and externally serialized. All13cost rows and seven equal-contract timing samples are present; unaided delayed assessment remains external. Bounded author support only."
